    },
    "on-the-path-or-off-it--image-27": {
      "id": "on-the-path-or-off-it--image-27",
      "type": "image",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "assetId": "on-the-path-or-off-it--asset",
      "alt": "Figure 3: the ten navigation moves, the four evidence-use labels, and a worked trajectory plotted as depth over rounds",
      "caption": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Figure 3: each round is reduced to its primary service and plotted by depth from the root cause; the worked run strays into the off-path band twice before it reaches the root at round 11."
        }
      ],
      "width": 100,
      "alignment": "center"
    },
    "on-the-path-or-off-it--scene": {
      "id": "on-the-path-or-off-it--scene",
      "type": "component",
      "definitionId": "on-the-path-or-off-it--definition",
      "parameters": {
        "alt": "Two runs plotted round by round against the fault's path: the correct run stays on the path, mostly acts on what it retrieves and reaches the root in 31 rounds; the failed run strays off the path, mostly ignores its results and ends off the path after 38."
      }
    },
    "three-ways-to-miss--text-37": {
      "id": "three-ways-to-miss--text-37",
      "type": "text",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "p-28",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two authors coded all 154 failed ThinkDepth.ai trajectories against the evidence each fault type requires (93.5% identical code sets). Twelve recurring modes fall into three families, by what happened to the decisive evidence:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "list-29",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "li-30",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-31",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Never gathered (OMIT).",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " Evidence reachable in telemetry is never queried: no healthy baseline, no span-level test of a claimed edge, no resource probe with concrete names, no peer ranking, no drill-down, no timing check."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-32",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-33",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Gathered, misread (MIS).",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " Silence read as health, the loudest victim blamed over a quieter culprit, caller and callee sides reversed."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-34",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-35",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Reasoning off the evidence (GEN).",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " An early hypothesis kept against later evidence, a cause outside the allowed states, a channel abandoned after an empty result."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-36",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Qwen fails mostly by omission (no resource probe in 63.5% of its failures), Sonnet mostly by misreading (wrong service-side semantics in 86.0%). On the held-out RCA100 benchmark all eleven comparable modes recur, and incorrect runs show 3.29 distinct modes on average against 0.71 for correct runs."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "three-ways-to-miss--image-38": {
      "id": "three-ways-to-miss--image-38",
      "type": "image",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "assetId": "three-ways-to-miss--asset",
      "alt": "Figure 6b: a disk fault on tidb-tikv-0 seen as a slow product page; the baseline blames the noisy Ad service, DiagGuard finds the storage node",
      "caption": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Figure 6b: a disk-I/O fault on the TiKV node tidb-tikv-0 surfaces only as product-page tail latency (p99 0.25 s → 10 s); the baseline anchors on Ad, whose errors are chronic noise, and never leaves the service tier."
        }
      ],
      "width": 100,
      "alignment": "center"
    },
    "three-ways-to-miss--scene": {
      "id": "three-ways-to-miss--scene",
      "type": "component",
      "definitionId": "three-ways-to-miss--definition",
      "parameters": {
        "alt": "On a held-out incident, a disk fault on tidb-tikv-0 shows only as a slow product page; the agent searches the service tier, blames the chronically noisy Ad service, and its six coded failures fall into three families."
      }
    },
    "guarded-runs-find-it--text-50": {
      "id": "guarded-runs-find-it--text-50",
      "type": "text",
      "only": [
        "web"
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "p-39",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "DiagGuard wraps an unchanged agent framework with two defenses traced to the three families: a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Verifier",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " that runs a diagnostic self-audit before the investigation and a soundness check before the answer, and a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Grounder",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " that profiles the actual telemetry before the first query. Both are added through prompts and tools, with rules fixed across settings."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "list-40",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "li-41",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-42",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Every configuration improves.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " ThinkDepth.ai on AIOps 2025 gains 6.5 points of Acc@1 under Qwen and 9.0 under Doubao; across 12 RCA100 configurations the median gain is 10.5 points, from 3.5 to 35.1 (mABC under Doubao, from a 3.5% baseline). Node F1 and Edge F1 rise in 11 of 12."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-43",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-44",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Failures become rarer.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " Distinct failure modes per run fall from 1.94 to 1.39 over 1,368 runs; seven modes drop significantly, such as untested edges (57.3% → 44.7%) and channels dropped after an empty result (15.1% → 4.7%)."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-45",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-46",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Each defense adds its share.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " On AIOps 2025 (Doubao, five runs) the Grounder alone adds 4.5 points, the Verifier alone 4.1, both together 9.0 (43.5% → 52.5%), at $0.16 per incident."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "li-47",
              "type": "listItem",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p-48",
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The framework sets the failure profile.",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " Failure profiles are more alike across backbones within one framework (cosine 0.950) than across frameworks (0.767)."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p-49",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A correct label says whether an agent localized the fault; its trajectory says whether the diagnosis is grounded, where it broke, and what to guard against."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
